abstract: >-
  MATLAB scripts, which also run in GNU Octave, solving the full Euler equations of irrotational surface gravity
  waves in deep water, written in conformal variables, by a Fourier pseudo-spectral method with an exponential filter,
  exact integration of the linear terms (integrating factor of Lawson) and an adaptive embedded Runge–Kutta scheme of
  Cash and Karp. The example is the Peregrine breather of the wave-tank experiment of Shemer and Alperovich (2013),
  followed from the wavemaker to the distance where the Peregrine solution has its maximum; the surface velocities and
  their horizontal derivatives can also be computed.
